# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-device runtime memory — NOT shared across devices.
#
# This repo plays two roles:
#   1) Meta-system definition (docs/, _System/, _index.md, README/CLAUDE.md)
#      → tracked, push/clone the skeleton across devices
#   2) Per-device runtime memory (Memory/*, Distilled/*, Knowledge/*, Agents/*)
#      → ignored, each device fills its own as Claude operates locally
#
# Only the _index.md inside each top-level area is tracked, so a fresh
# clone shows the structure and Claude can self-orient. Everything else
# under those areas is the device's own brain content.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Memory — per-device runtime
Memory/**
!Memory/_index.md
!Memory/*/
!Memory/*/_index.md

# Stop-hook output (Decisions, Mistakes, Patterns) + manual Sessions — per-device
Decisions/**
!Decisions/_index.md
Mistakes/**
!Mistakes/_index.md
Patterns/**
!Patterns/_index.md
Sessions/**
!Sessions/_index.md

# Knowledge — per-device, except the index
Knowledge/**
!Knowledge/_index.md
!Knowledge/*/
!Knowledge/*/_index.md

# Agents — per-device, except the index
Agents/**
!Agents/_index.md

# _System/audit — per-device weekly/monthly audit results
_System/audit/

# macOS
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Obsidian temp/runtime
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/app.json
.obsidian/appearance.json
.obsidian/graph.json

# Trash
.trash/

# Nested vault accident prevention (adjust to your own notes vault's folder
# name if you ever nest it inside this repo by mistake)
MyVault/

# Conflict files (obsidian-git)
conflict-files-obsidian-git.md

# Large binaries — consider Git LFS if needed
*.mp4
*.zip
Attachments/*.png
Attachments/*.jpg
Attachments/*.gif

# bkit local metadata
docs/.bkit-memory.json
docs/.pdca-status.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# check-purity's local proper-noun wordlist — never ship your own project's
# real company/person/vault names. tools/denylist.local.txt.example (tracked)
# shows the format; your real copy stays local.
tools/*.local.txt
